{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections#lem:dc-ch2-2-2-c-coord","title":"lem:dc-ch2-2-2-c-coord","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections.md","line":42,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections.tex#lem:dc-ch2-2-2-c-coord","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections#lem:dc-ch2-2-2-coord]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections#def:dc-ch2-3-7-christoffel]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections.tex","label":"lem:dc-ch2-2-2-c-coord","line":87,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[property (c) in coordinates: induced fields]\n  \\label{lem:dc-ch2-2-2-c-coord}\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch2-2-2-coord, def:dc-ch2-3-7-christoffel}\n\n  \\dcref{ch2:2.2}\n  For a coordinate vector field $Y$ and a tangent vector $v$ at $y$, define\n  \\[\n    (\\nabla_vY)(y)=DY(y)v+\\Gamma(v,Y(y))(y).\n  \\]\n  If $V=Y\\circ u$ along a coordinate curve $u$, then\n  \\[\n    \\frac{D}{dt}(Y\\circ u)=(\\nabla_{\\dot u}Y)(u).\n  \\]\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n  \\sketch\n  The chain rule gives $(Y\\circ u)'=DY(u)\\dot u$, and the Christoffel terms in\n  the two expressions coincide.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[property (c) in coordinates: induced fields] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368322d322d322d632d636f6f7264\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections%23lem%3Adc-ch2-2-2-coord\">↗ lem:dc-ch2-2-2-coord</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections%23def%3Adc-ch2-3-7-christoffel\">↗ def:dc-ch2-3-7-christoffel</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch2:2.2</span></span>For a coordinate vector field <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$Y$\">$Y$</span> and a tangent vector <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$v$\">$v$</span> at <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$y$\">$y$</span>, define <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  (\\nabla _vY)(y)=DY(y)v+\\Gamma (v,Y(y))(y).  \\]\">\\[  (\\nabla _vY)(y)=DY(y)v+\\Gamma (v,Y(y))(y).  \\]</span> If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$V=Y\\circ u$\">$V=Y\\circ u$</span> along a coordinate curve <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$u$\">$u$</span>, then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  \\frac{D}{dt}(Y\\circ u)=(\\nabla _{\\dot u}Y)(u).  \\]\">\\[  \\frac{D}{dt}(Y\\circ u)=(\\nabla _{\\dot u}Y)(u).  \\]</span>  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch The chain rule gives <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(Y\\circ u)&#x27;=DY(u)\\dot u$\">$(Y\\circ u)&#x27;=DY(u)\\dot u$</span>, and the Christoffel terms in the two expressions coincide. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections#lem:dc-ch2-2-2-coord","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections#lem:dc-ch2-2-2-c-formula10","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_AffineConnectionsRiemannianConnections#lem:dc-ch2-2-